# Test Flow: Register → Verify OTP → Login → Password Reset → Reset Password

@base_url = http://localhost:5103/api
@auth_url = http://localhost:5103/api/auth

# TEST DATA - UPDATE THESE FOR YOUR TESTING

@test_email_1 = mctechnologies26@gmail.com
@test_email_2 = testuser2@gmail.com
@test_email_3 = testuser3@gmail.com
@test_password = NewPassword789!
@test_first_name = Muyonga
@test_last_name = Lugadilu
@test_phone = 0714665512

//ADMIN USER (For testing SuperAdmin-only endpoints)
@admin_email = admin@ticketing.com
@admin_password = Admin@12345

//TEAMLEAD USER (For testing TeamLead-only endpoints)
@teamlead_email = teamlead1@ticketing.com
@teamlead_password = Admin@12345

//TECHNICIAN USER (For testing Technician-only endpoints)
@technician_email = technician1@ticketing.com
@technician_password = Admin@12345


# IMPORTANT: Update after successful login
@customer_token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..AGFJtXLMQqWFStTfMt3pB0iUiXL3VUcoTZQeeHUoCqU

# SECTION 1: REGISTRATION - CUSTOMER SELF-REGISTRATION

### 1.1 Register New Customer (Sends OTP to email)
POST {{auth_url}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "password": "{{test_password}}",
  "firstName": "{{test_first_name}}",
  "lastName": "{{test_last_name}}",
  "phoneNumber": "{{test_phone}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - OTP sent to email, account created but not verified

###

### 1.2 Register with Duplicate Email (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "password": "{{test_password}}",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Smith"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Email already registered"

### 1.3 Register with Invalid Email (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "invalid-email",
  "password": "{{test_password}}",
  "firstName": "{{test_first_name}}",
  "lastName": "{{test_last_name}}"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Invalid email format"

### 1.4 Register with Weak Password (No Special Char)
POST {{auth_url}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test.weak@gmail.com",
  "password": "WeakPassword123",
  "firstName": "{{test_first_name}}",
  "lastName": "{{test_last_name}}"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Password must contain special character"

### 1.5 Register with Short Password (Less than 8 chars)
POST {{auth_url}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test.short@gmail.com",
  "password": "Short1!",
  "firstName": "{{test_first_name}}",
  "lastName": "{{test_last_name}}"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Password must be at least 8 characters"

### 1.6 Register with Missing Required Field
POST {{auth_url}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "test.missing@gmail.com",
  "password": "{{test_password}}"
}

# Expected: 400 Bad Request - "First name and last name are required"

# SECTION 2: OTP VERIFICATION
POST {{auth_url}}/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "otp": "611787"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - Email verified, account activated
### 2.2 Verify with Wrong OTP (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "otp": "999999"
}


### 2.3 Verify with Expired OTP (Should Fail)
### Wait 10+ minutes after registration, then run this
POST {{auth_url}}/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 2.4 Verify Non-existent Email (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@gmail.com",
  "otp": "000000"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "User not found"

# SECTION 3: RESEND OTP

### 3.1 Resend OTP (If original expired or lost)
POST {{auth_url}}/resend-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}"
}

### 3.2 Resend OTP to Non-existent Email (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/resend-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@gmail.com"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "User not found"

###

### 3.3 Resend OTP to Already Verified Email (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/resend-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "User already verified"





# SECTION 4: LOGIN - NORMAL LOGIN WITH EMAIL/PASSWORD


### 4.1 Login with Correct Credentials
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "password": "{{test_password}}"
}

### ADMIN LOGIN (For testing SuperAdmin-only endpoints)
###
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{admin_email}}",
  "password": "{{admin_password}}"
}

### TeamLead LOGIN (For testing TeamLead-only endpoints)
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{teamlead_email}}",
  "password": "{{teamlead_password}}"
}

### Technician Login
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{technician_email}}",
  "password": "{{technician_password}}"
}
### Expected: 200 OK - Returns JWT token, user info, expiration time
### IMPORTANT: Copy token from response and update @customer_token variable above

### 4.2 Login with Non-existent Email (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@gmail.com",
  "password": "{{test_password}}"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - "Invalid email or password"

###

### 4.3 Login with Wrong Password (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "password": "WrongPassword123!"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - "Invalid email or password"

###

### 4.4 Login Before Email Verification (Should Fail)
### Register new user but don't verify OTP first
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_2}}",
  "password": "{{test_password}}"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - "Email not verified"

###


# SECTION 5: PASSWORD RESET - 6 DIGIT CODE FLOW


### 5.1 Request Password Reset Code (Sends 6-digit code to email)
POST {{auth_url}}/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - 6-digit reset code sent to email
### IMPORTANT: Check email for reset code

###

### 5.2 Request Reset Code for Non-existent Email (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nonexistent@gmail.com"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "User not found"

###

### 5.3 Resend Password Reset Code (If first code expired)
POST {{auth_url}}/resend-password-reset-code
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - New 6-digit code sent to email

###


# SECTION 6: RESET PASSWORD - WITH 6-DIGIT CODE


### 6.1 Reset Password with Valid Code
### STEP 1: Get 6-digit code from email (from section 5.1)
### STEP 2: Replace "000000" with actual code
POST {{auth_url}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "resetCode": "872457",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword789!",
  "confirmPassword": "NewPassword789!"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - Password changed successfully

###

### 6.2 Reset Password with Invalid Code (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "resetCode": "999999",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword789!",
  "confirmPassword": "NewPassword789!"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Invalid reset code"

###

### 6.3 Reset Password with Expired Code (Should Fail)
### Wait 10+ minutes after requesting code, then run
POST {{auth_url}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "resetCode": "000000",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword789!",
  "confirmPassword": "NewPassword789!"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Reset code expired"

###

### 6.4 Reset Password with Mismatched Passwords (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "resetCode": "000000",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword789!",
  "confirmPassword": "DifferentPassword123!"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Passwords do not match"

###

### 6.5 Reset Password with Weak Password (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "resetCode": "000000",
  "newPassword": "WeakPassword123",
  "confirmPassword": "WeakPassword123"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Password must contain special character"

###

### 6.6 Reset Password with Invalid Code Format (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "resetCode": "12345",
  "newPassword": "NewPassword789!",
  "confirmPassword": "NewPassword789!"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Reset code must be 6 digits"

###


# SECTION 7: LOGIN WITH NEW PASSWORD (After Reset)


### 7.1 Login with New Password
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "password": "NewPassword789!"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - Returns JWT token with new password

###

### 7.2 Login with Old Password (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{test_email_1}}",
  "password": "{{test_password}}"
}

### Expected: 401 Unauthorized - "Invalid email or password"

###

# SECTION 8: ACCEPTED INVITATION (For invited users like TeamLead, Technician)


### 8.1 Accept Invitation (For invited users)
### Get invitationToken from email sent by SuperAdmin/TeamLead
POST {{auth_url}}/accept-invitation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invitationToken": "your-token-from-email",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Expected: 200 OK - Returns JWT token for immediate login

###

### 8.2 Accept Invitation with Invalid Token (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/accept-invitation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invitationToken": "invalid-token",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Invalid invitation token"

###

### 8.3 Accept Expired Invitation (Should Fail)
### Wait 7+ days, then try
POST {{auth_url}}/accept-invitation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invitationToken": "your-token-from-email",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "Invitation expired"

###

### 8.4 Accept Already Accepted Invitation (Should Fail)
POST {{auth_url}}/accept-invitation
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "invitationToken": "your-token-from-email",
  "password": "SecurePass123!",
  "confirmPassword": "SecurePass123!"
}

### Expected: 400 Bad Request - "This invitation has already been accepted"

###

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# COMPLETE TEST WORKFLOW
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# RECOMMENDED TEST SEQUENCE:
#
# 1. Section 1.1 - Register new customer
# 2. Check email for OTP
# 3. Section 2.1 - Verify OTP
# 4. Section 4.1 - Login with credentials
# 5. Copy token and update @customer_token
# 6. Section 5.1 - Request password reset
# 7. Check email for reset code
# 8. Section 6.1 - Reset password with code
# 9. Section 7.1 - Login with new password
#
# Test error cases by running sections 1.2-1.6, 2.2-2.4, 4.2-4.4, 6.2-6.6
#
# Expected: All success tests return 200 OK, all error tests return appropriate 400/401

###
